d","size":4246017,"digest":"sha256:14ccd51171feff7b58f45563db0f689fce4d163a7dc8fc841e06fee880961320","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-26T01:44:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T01:44:47Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/thatsmethen/relink/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.20261026-relink/ReLink-Windows-development.zip"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thatsmethen/relink/releases/assets/676673916","id":676673916,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVUvrfc4oVTl8","name":"SHA256SUMS.txt","label":"","uploader":{"login":"thatsmethen","id":115801388,"node_id":"U_kgDOBub9LA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115801388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen","html_url":"https://github.com/thatsmethen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thatsmethen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":627,"digest":"sha256:5ac887ab7f440a0168e094d5b6725e9e92ecb565837434f0b15e5658173398ed","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-26T01:45:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T01:45:01Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/thatsmethen/relink/releases/download/v0.1.0-preview.20261026-relink/SHA256SUMS.txt"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thatsmethen/relink/tarball/v0.1.0-preview.20261026-relink","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/thatsmethen/relink/zipball/v0.1.0-preview.20261026-relink","body":"ReLink's development preview now saves explicit output routes with the studio. Assign a mix to each device and choose one clock; selecting a different mix in the editor leaves those assignments intact. The Rust runtime connects simultaneous CoreAudio/WASAPI outputs with independent clock compensation and per-device control submission status.\n\nAlso included: recovery saves preserve the original file before replacement, saved recovery work reopens normally, late cleanup failures remain visible after Stop, and startup priming has separate bounded timing allowances.\n\n![Current ReLink mixer](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thatsmethen/relink/e552ed967db17bb0096d9f03251d8d917a0ac85b/docs/screenshots/mixer-macos.png)\n\n[Output routing screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thatsmethen/relink/e552ed967db17bb0096d9f03251d8d917a0ac85b/docs/screenshots/output-routing-macos.png) · [Mix effects](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thatsmethen/relink/e552ed967db17bb0096d9f03251d8d917a0ac85b/docs/screenshots/mix-effects-macos.png)\n\nSource: `902118a60b070bb9cefdef75d5b477b5350b9847`. [Desktop CI](https://github.com/thatsmethen/relink/actions/runs/40254943747) passed on macOS 15 and Windows Server 2022. Local unchanged-source verification passed 253 tests. The screenshots are actual stopped macOS views from a debug build of that same source, with explicit test tones; they do not depict live audio.\n\n**Development preview, not production audio qualification.** The separate [installed single-output observation](https://github.com/thatsmethen/relink/actions/runs/40254943736) failed both its HAL and runtime jobs. Earlier intermittent failures remain unresolved. Installed simultaneous-output PCM and native Windows audio/interaction remain unqualified.\n\nDownloads are app-only: macOS Apple silicon is ad-hoc signed without notarization; Windows x64 is unsigned. No virtual-driver installer is included. Both packages embed the original ReLink icon and matching dependency notices. Existing internal identifiers and studio paths remain compatible; legacy studio files load without modification until saved.\n\n`SHA256SUMS.txt` covers both original CI package ZIPs, all three screenshots, the icon and verification report. The report distinguishes package checks from runtime acceptance. First-party code remains proprietary despite public repository visibility.\n"}